---
layout: layouts/base.njk
bodyClass: "ind-page"
---
{#
  Layout for the industry pages — /ai-training-<industry>/.

  These are commercial pages, not articles, so they are deliberately not built on
  layouts/resource.njk: no byline, no breadcrumb into the resource library, and a
  call to action rather than "keep reading".

  The whole point of an industry page is the part that could not be written for
  any other industry. So `useCases` and `concern` carry the weight, and the shared
  program section below is kept short — a page that is 80% boilerplate with the
  sector's name swapped in is the thin-content pattern these are supposed to avoid.

  Front matter each page supplies:
    title, description, permalink, industry, h1, eyebrow, lede,
    painsHeading, pains: [str], useCasesHeading, useCasesLede,
    useCases: [{title, body}], concern: {heading, body},
    faq: [{q, a}], reading: [{url, label}], closer
#}
<main class="ind">

  <section>
    <p class="ind-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow or "AI training" }}</p>
    <h1>{{ h1 }}</h1>
    <p class="ind-lede">{{ lede | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/programs/">See the program</a>
    </div>
    <p class="ind-trust">
      Ad On Group has been Australian-owned since 2008 and is rated 4.8 from 229 Google
      reviews. Our AI training is delivered by Claude Certified Associates, and 40+
      Australian businesses have completed the program.
    </p>
  </section>

  {# Sector proof. Deliberately says Ad On Group *works with* these businesses,
     which is true across the group's services — not that each has completed the
     AI training, which would be a different and unevidenced claim. #}
  {% if clients %}
  <section>
    <h2>We already work in this sector</h2>
    <p>{{ clients | safe }}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if pains and pains.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ painsHeading }}</h2>
    <ul class="ind-list">
      {% for p in pains %}<li>{{ p | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if useCases and useCases.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ useCasesHeading or "What your team would actually use it for" }}</h2>
    {% if useCasesLede %}<p>{{ useCasesLede | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    <div class="ind-grid">
      {% for u in useCases %}
      <article class="ind-card">
        <h3>{{ u.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ u.body | safe }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if concern %}
  <section>
    <div class="ind-note">
      <h2>{{ concern.heading }}</h2>
      {{ concern.body | safe }}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>How the training works</h2>
    <p>
      Three months, 24 modules, around two hours a week, self-paced so it fits around
      {{ industry }} work rather than pulling people off the tools for a day. It runs in
      three stages: getting fluent with the tools, automating the tasks that repeat, then
      building AI agents that handle a slice of a job end to end.
    </p>
    <p>
      What we teach is tool-agnostic. Your team learns the thinking, then applies it in
      ChatGPT, Copilot, Gemini or Claude — so the skills survive whichever tool your
      practice standardises on next year. <a href="/ongoing-support/">Ongoing support</a>
      comes with every program: monthly webinars, tool masterclasses, a support hour and
      an active community, because the tools keep moving after the course ends.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ai-quiz/">Take the free AI audit</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if faq and faq.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>Questions {{ industry }} teams ask</h2>
    {% for item in faq %}
    <details>
      <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
      <div><p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p></div>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if reading and reading.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>Worth reading first</h2>
    <div class="ind-more">
      {% for r in reading %}<a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# The free session paired with this sector. A webinar is the low-commitment
     entry point for someone who is not ready to talk to anyone yet, and it is
     also the only thing here that carries a date — which is what makes it worth
     linking from a page that otherwise never changes. #}
  {% for w in webinarSchedule.upcoming %}{% if w.industry == page.url %}
  <section>
    <h2>There's a free session on this</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="{{ w.url }}">{{ w.title }}</a> &mdash; {{ w.pretty }}, {{ w.prettyTime }}.
      Free, online, 45 minutes, open to anyone. {{ w.blurb }}
    </p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="{{ w.url }}">Details and registration</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}

  {# Industry × location. The pairing is the point: "AI training for accounting
     firms in Brisbane" is a question almost nobody has written a page for, and
     it is where a page like this can win while the head term stays out of reach.

     `localAngle` is a real observation about that sector in these areas, not a
     list of city names wearing a sentence — a stuffed list reads as spam to a
     person and adds nothing for a crawler either. Locations render as plain text
     until their own page exists (`hasPage`), so nothing here 404s. #}
  <section>
    <h2>Where we work</h2>
    <p>
      We're based on the Gold Coast and the program runs online and self-paced, so where
      you are doesn't change what your team gets. Most of our face-to-face work is across
      South East Queensland and Northern NSW, plus Adelaide, where we have an office.
    </p>
    {% if localAngle %}<p>{{ localAngle | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    <div class="ind-more">
      {% for l in locations.items %}
        {% if l.hasPage %}<a href="/ai-training-{{ l.slug }}/">{{ l.name }}</a>
        {% else %}<span class="ind-place">{{ l.name }}{% if l.note %} <em>&middot; {{ l.note }}</em>{% endif %}</span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {# Cross-links, driven off _data/industries.json so adding a seventh page needs
     no edit here and none of the six goes stale. The current page is filtered
     out rather than rendered as a link to itself. #}
  <section>
    <h2>We train other sectors too</h2>
    <div class="ind-more">
      {% for i in industries.items %}{% if i.url != page.url %}
      <a href="{{ i.url }}">{{ i.label }}</a>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>{{ closerHeading or "Get your team started" }}</h2>
    <p>{{ closer | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ad-on-ai-division/">About Ad On AI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
